method.description:
A [NetwAction] for an action such as firing or placing something, bound to [param authority] the server runs to judge it.
Repeated calls return the same [NetwAction].
[codeblock]
@onready var place_bomb := Netw.action(_place_bomb)

func _ready() -> void:
    place_bomb.predict = _show_bomb_now

func _place_bomb(ctx: NetwActionContext) -> void:
    var bomb := BOMB.instantiate()
    ctx.bind(bomb)
    bombs.add_child(bomb)
[/codeblock]
The server judges an action before other peers see it. To let a client spawn, move and despawn a node first and have the server confirm it later, see [member NetwEntity.lifecycle].

Opens [param path] and moves players to it. [param scope] says who moves. Their nodes do not move, so spawn them in the [NetwScene] the promise gives.
[codeblock]
func start_match() -> void:
    Netw.change_scene_to_file(self, "res://match.tscn").then(spawn_players)

func spawn_players(arena: NetwScene) -> void:
    for player: NetwPlayer in arena.viewers:
        arena.root.add_child(Netw.spawn_player(player, make_player))
[/codeblock]
On a client this is a request that [method configure_scene_requests] decides, and it is rejected when there is none. The promise then gives [constant @GlobalScope.OK].

Declares extra configuration for [param callable] that [annotation @GDScript.@rpc] does not cover.
[codeblock]
func _init() -> void:
    Netw.configure_rpc(self.aim).controller().quantize(
            NetwQuantizeAngle.new().bits(12).centered(),
    )

@rpc("any_peer", "unreliable")
func aim(yaw: float) -> void:
    turret.rotation.y = yaw
[/codeblock]

Lets clients request a scene change. [param handler] runs on the server for every request and returns [constant @GlobalScope.OK] to allow it.
[codeblock]
func _init() -> void:
    Netw.configure_scene_requests(authorize_scene_request)

func authorize_scene_request(
    player: NetwPlayer,
    destination: String,
    scope: NetwScene.SceneChange
) -> Error:
    if scope != NetwScene.SCENE_CHANGE_PLAYER:
        return ERR_UNAUTHORIZED
    return OK if unlocked(player, destination) else ERR_UNAUTHORIZED
[/codeblock]

Picks which entities outlive a server transfer in [constant NetwSession.TRANSFER_REJOIN]. The new server calls [param keep] with the root node of each entity it took over, and despawns the ones it answers [code]false[/code] for before any client gets the world again.
[codeblock]
func _init() -> void:
    Netw.configure_transfer(keeps)

func keeps(node: Node) -> bool:
    return not node.is_in_group(&"loot")
[/codeblock]
Declare it on every peer, since any of them can become the server.

Returns a copy of the state of [param entity] at [param tick]. It is empty when nothing was recorded.
[codeblock]
func _place_bomb(ctx: NetwActionContext, pos: Vector2) -> void:
    var past := Netw.sample(entity, ctx.view_tick)
    if not past.has_value(&"position"):
        ctx.deny()
        return
[/codeblock]

Returns the multiplayer scene [param node] is in. Use [method NetwSession.find_scene] to find one by name.
[codeblock]
var here := Netw.scene(self)
var track := Netw.session(self).find_scene(&"Track")
[/codeblock]
